FixDeform::update_box (src/fix_deform.cpp:892-916) calls update_domain(), which at src/fix_deform.cpp:1243 does `domain->x2lamda(atom->nlocal, groupbit)` and at src/fix_deform.cpp:1279 `domain->lamda2x(atom->nlocal, groupbit)`. Both are overridden by DomainKokkos (domain_kokkos.h:40,42); DomainKokkos::lamda2x(int,int) (domain_kokkos.cpp:625-642) runs a device kernel and ends with `atomKK->modified(Device,X_MASK)`. atomKK->modified(Host,ALL_MASK) then reaches TransformView::modify_host -> Kokkos::DualView::modify_host (kokkos_type.h:878-886, k_x is a TransformView with NEED_TRANSFORM==0 for the default double build, kokkos_type.h:700,1257), so the host modify counter becomes device+1 and the next `sync(Device,X_MASK)` deep-copies host->device. auto_sync is 0 during a run (verlet_kokkos.cpp:311) and FixDeformKokkos sets datamask_read/modify = EMPTY_MASK (fix_deform_kokkos.cpp:33-34), so ModifyKokkos::end_of_step (modify_kokkos.cpp:440-453) does not re-sync either. The sibling override migrate_atoms() (fix_deform_kokkos.cpp:62-67) is safe only because there the device write (x2lamda) happens BEFORE the sync, and the file's own comment at lines 49-53 documents exactly this hazard for pre_exchange().
